{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1014274-keep-hunt-intersting","id":1014274,"title":"Keep hunt intersting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-08T06:22:28-08:00","id":1014274,"title":"Keep hunt intersting","content":"Hi all,<br /> I'd need some tips to keep hunts intersting and tematically strong for my PCs. Now, after a year of play, they reached a considerable level of power (personoal at least). They have at least 8-9 point in disciplines so it's quite impossible for me keep high the tension. They have Majesty, Dominate, Obfuscate so, in one way or another, seems silly to mee let them roll for the haunt when they said me: I go in a pub and use majesty to seduce someone and take in a secluded place; or when, with obfuscate, I fallow a lonely man and when he is in a dark alley I'll bite him. <br /> <br /> \u200bCan you give me some tips? I just cannot let someone pass there casually too often. This results in: &quot;Ok before to go there I feed up.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T06:41:46-08:00","id":1014283,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how well they deal with loose ends, but: hunters and masquerade breaches are always a good threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T07:14:18-08:00","id":1014301,"title":"","content":"Have you tried the diceless hunting method?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, by RAW, Disciplines don't guarantee success on with-dice hunting rolls. They just add your dots in the Discipline to your dice pool at the cost of 1 Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-08-2016, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T07:29:22-08:00","id":1014305,"title":"","content":"sudden surprise as your victim is drugged, or as his blood tastes funny (he's a supernatural of a different type), or when he was already low health (due to past experiences of whatever) and he quickly passes out, or he's noticed by someone as he feeds, or his strange pattern is noticed and someone calls him out. For example: He's in a pub, middle of seducting someone with Majesty, as he's about to leave one of his past victims run up &quot;Hey, you asshole, you didn't call me after YESTERDAY and you'r enow hooking up with someone new?&quot; <br /> <br /> All of these and more can be used to create surprises","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T08:06:47-08:00","id":1014316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1014274-keep-hunt-intersting?p=1014301#post1014301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you tried the diceless hunting method?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, by RAW, Disciplines don't guarantee success on with-dice hunting rolls. They just add your dots in the Discipline to your dice pool at the cost of 1 Vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>I explained myself badly. What I meant is that they don't need to make the hunt rolls. They just say to me: I go there, use Majesty 2 (that by raw let the victim willing give you also his car or money) and take a man/woman in a safe place to eat. <br /> Now, yes, I should roll to see if the power is succesful but, it's no sense due to the fact that, even with an unlucky roll the PC could use it on another victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 12-08-2016, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T08:25:37-08:00","id":1014324,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, and my interpretation might be off the actual rules, hunt rolls are meant to take into account a few things. Time finding where to go, selecting the proper victim, secluding them, using whatever power/skill/etc to actually subdue them for feeding. So if you fail, I think the idea is that you really don\u2019t have the time to take care of all these things. And that feeding isn\u2019t typically always as easy as, \u2018I follow a lonely man down an alley.\u2019 Sometimes lonely men just aren\u2019t walking down nearby allies. Properly pulling off a stealthy feeding is more work to me. They shouldn't get easy second chances if they blew it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T11:28:53-08:00","id":1014391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1014274-keep-hunt-intersting?p=1014316#post1014316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I explained myself badly. What I meant is that they don't need to make the hunt rolls. They just say to me: I go there, use Majesty 2 (that by raw let the victim willing give you also his car or money) and take a man/woman in a safe place to eat.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just not how feeding works by RAW. It seems to me like you're allowing your players to circumvent the hunting mechanics, and then facing an issue with players not needing to hunt. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1014274-keep-hunt-intersting?p=1014316#post1014316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, yes, I should roll to see if the power is succesful but, it's no sense due to the fact that, even with an unlucky roll the PC could use it on another victim.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's precisely why feeding is done via hunting rolls (or diceless hunting) instead of just using Discipline powers on random passersby. You abstract the entire process of searching for a suitable vessel, attempting to beguile them with your Disciplines, and repeating until you score, into a single dice roll. The book recommends adding penalties for each failure, personally I prefer failure on hunting rolls to mean eventual success at finding a vessel, but with complications. Or you could use the diceless version, which might work better for you if you want to get into the nitty gritty of each individual interaction when feeding, rather than making it highly abstract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T11:51:32-08:00","id":1014400,"title":"","content":"I've found they're a really good place to offer beats in exchange for a dramatic failure, like getting caught on CCTV or in one game the victim turned out to be a hunter leading the Vampire, my group does the same as Charlaquin with normal failures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T11:57:29-08:00","id":1014404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1014274-keep-hunt-intersting?p=1014316#post1014316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I explained myself badly. What I meant is that they don't need to make the hunt rolls. They just say to me: I go there, use Majesty 2 (that by raw let the victim willing give you also his car or money) and take a man/woman in a safe place to eat.</div> </div> </div> </div>As careless as that is they're practically begging you for a surprise to happen.<br /> <br /> You just bilked another, more powerful vampire's ghoul or living family member. A mage. The son of the commander of Task Force Valkyrie. A Beast. Someone infected with the ragged-men virus.<br /> <br /> You said you want to keep hunts 'thematically strong,' what is the theme for your game? What challenges are they facing that they've gained all these Disciplines and just randomly pick people to feed on without a second thought?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T12:07:27-08:00","id":1014409,"title":"","content":"I would even give the feeding targets some unique personality quirks. Not enough to make them characters, unless one of the players takes a fancy to them, but just something to remind the players that they're still feeding from other human beings. If nothing else it would add some drama to the hunting scenes.<br /> <br /> Like the above mentioned Majesty targeted club goer could be super anti-social and only there because their friends forced them to be their designated driver so the whole seduction scene is suuuuuper awkward. Or the lone Obfuscate target could get jumped before the player can get them and it's revealed they're in deep with the mob.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 12-08-2016, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T12:33:21-08:00","id":1014412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1014274-keep-hunt-intersting?p=1014404#post1014404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You said you want to keep hunts 'thematically strong,' what is the theme for your game? What challenges are they facing that they've gained all these Disciplines and just randomly pick people to feed on without a second thought?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are moved in this new city just recentely and with thematically strong I meant that, according to me, the hunt for a vampire should be something to &quot;enjoy&quot; by both the character and the player, but with the &quot;automatic success&quot; given by disciplines, often is easyer, for lazy player, just say: I go in that bar at the slum enchant someone and take him in the dark alley outside. I just would like to find a way to keep high the drama of the moment and I would like the player could been incentivate to don't see the hunt just a way to fill up their blood pools.<br /> <br /> @Dusksage: I like your tips and I'm gooing to try to use it.<br /> <br /> @Charlaquin: I got your point but, how could I say: &quot;no you can't just get there using majesty&quot; to a player that say this? I would like to induce them to &quot;want&quot; play the hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T12:45:05-08:00","id":1014424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1014274-keep-hunt-intersting?p=1014412#post1014412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Charlaquin: I got your point but, how could I say: &quot;no you can't just get there using majesty&quot; to a player that say this? I would like to induce them to &quot;want&quot; play the hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the player says &quot;I go in that bar at the slum enchant someone and take him in the dark alley outside&quot;, you say, &quot;Ok, spend a Vitae and roll Presence + Persuasion + Majesty, (+ Hunting Grounds if they have it and are in their feeding territory).&quot; If they succeed, narrate the scene of who they find, what he's like, how he reacts to their advances, etc. and then let them take as much Vitae as they want (keeping in mind that more than about 2 is going to leave the guy pretty messed up, and 7 will almost definitely kill him). If they fail, narrate the same results, but add a complication. Maybe his blood is drugged and they get a Condition. Maybe he turns out to be a Wolf-Blooded and his pack shows up to rescue him. Maybe this is another vampire's hunting territory and she happen to turn up just as they are about to sink their teeth into him; or heck, maybe she's a Carthian and Lex Terrae triggers, staining their mouth black. maybe there's a gang fight going down in the alley they picked. Just introduce some kind of complication as a result of the failed hunting roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-08-2016, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T13:41:23-08:00","id":1014442,"title":"","content":"The diceless hunting as Charlaquin stated would seem to be worth trying if you're into that. The hunting with dice mechanic seems incredibly harsh, though. not only do you have to spend vitae to use a discipline even though they all have a first level that doesn't need vitae, but doing that turns failure into dramatic failure. By contrast, you play a ventrue PC going into a bar, sitting in front of a customer, dominate 1 &quot;follow me&quot;, then feed, then &quot;nothing happened&quot;, &quot;go home&quot;. Done. No vitae spend and almost no risk of anything going really wrong.<br /> <br /> Now, while I see the problem, is it really one ? After a year of play, should the hunt still be a major part of play ? I don't really see anything wrong in the players going over it within a minute and then going back to whatever it is they were doing. Not everything has to be risky and dramatic all the time. Sometimes, the players just want to replenish vitae because they're low.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want to remind them of the consequences, and feel they're a bit too feed happy, maybe you could drop hints after the act. Player A feeds in a club one night with majesty, business as usual,the next day, they see an article or a facebook post or whatever about young guy at a party who collapsed and is in a coma due to severe anemia, then article goes on about how young people are too careless and go to parties even while sick of weakened. They see the photo/name of the guy and may recognize their victim. Facing the weirdness of being a predator is one thing, but it's yet another thing to realize you're so used to it, you start getting sloppy and causing damage without realizing. Aside from, that, to add to the complications, wouldn't a majesty hunting vampire end up building a reputation as a heartbreaker ? It's not a discrete power. Like it's been said, one victim may recognize the vampire with someone else and make a scene, but what if another old prey comes in, then another. The vampire might get banned from a few places because while they're really charming, after a while, everybody knows they're bad news.<br /> <br /> <br /> But personally I don't really bother much with feeding after a while. I mean, we get the idea. Vampire goes clubbing, is an hypocritical asshole and plays people like fiddles. It's a different thing when they're under pressure. The hunt becomes much more tense and there's more at stake when the vampire HAS to get vitae, right now. PC gets a call from a contact saying a rival vampire has had enough of their bullshit and is coming to kick their ass. Problem is, at that particular time, PC is almost dry. Can they get enough blood to not be caught with their pants down before the rival comes kicking down their (or their friends') door ? Later, the incident is over and the rival left the PC alone. Thing is they used every last bit of their vitae to drive them off, and now, they're maybe one hour from dawn. Can they manage to get some blood without frenzying before going to sleep ?<br /> <br /> By the same principle, you can play a few hunting scenes and progressively get harder, oddly. PCs find out they're explicitly banned from a few bars they used to go to, some knuckleheads decide to pick a fight with them, they get pulled over by cops who find an excuse to bring them in, making them waste time. Over time, the players might understand that someone is trying to mess with their unlives. Is it another vampire trying to prevent them from feeding before they attack them at their weakest, a hunter cell closing in on them ?<br /> <br /> Hunting can be a time for you to drop information in the background that's relevant to what's happening. The feeding itself is without risk, but stuff is happening on the side that the players might to pay attention to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}